usage: sample.py [-h] --method
                 {base,pi,ntk,ntk2,yarn,dype,yarn_temp,sega,sega_official,sega_static,sega_official_static,constancy,temp_only,constancy_nogate,constancy_sref,constancy_tm,constancy_tm_nogate}
                 --res HxW --prompts PROMPTS [--start START] [--end END]
                 [--seed SEED] [--steps STEPS] [--guidance GUIDANCE] --out OUT
                 [--profile PROFILE]
                 [--sega-static-profile SEGA_STATIC_PROFILE] [--eta ETA]
                 [--gate {on,off}] [--target {profile,slope}]
                 [--temperature {logN,sref,none}] [--device DEVICE]
                 [--cpu-offload] [--allow-download]

Generate one resumable FLUX campaign chunk.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --method {base,pi,ntk,ntk2,yarn,dype,yarn_temp,sega,sega_official,sega_static,sega_official_static,constancy,temp_only,constancy_nogate,constancy_sref,constancy_tm,constancy_tm_nogate}
  --res HxW
  --prompts PROMPTS
  --start START
  --end END
  --seed SEED
  --steps STEPS
  --guidance GUIDANCE
  --out OUT
  --profile PROFILE
  --sega-static-profile SEGA_STATIC_PROFILE
  --eta ETA
  --gate {on,off}       constancy_tm visibility gate; off selects
                        constancy_tm_nogate
  --target {profile,slope}
  --temperature {logN,sref,none}
  --device DEVICE
  --cpu-offload         Use only if the ordinary GPU run exhausts VRAM
  --allow-download      Allow missing FLUX cache files to download
